  "notes": "Drawn from 2024 photos of N8660A. Belly not seen squarely: the red is taken to run under the aft fuselage and the blue under the nose, as the sides show. Re-checked 2026-11-15: the fin is the state jets' Heart fin, as re-measured on Colorado One (N8690A, the same 737-800 fin): copied from there with its 'Southwest' title and flag. 'Lone Star One' measured on the 2024 left photo against the nose and the forward door (2.2-3.3 m back, x 0.057-0.087), two weights, so a pair of titles per side; its height and its line under the cockpit windows are Colorado One's, where the title sits in the same place.",
  "history": "Lone Star One since 1990: N352SW (737-300), then N931WN (737-700), now N8660A."
}
